# Cell from playpick: mode=walk, boss=whisper, spec=priest:shadow,
# style=mash, size=10, difficulty=normal, view=390x844,touch, save=fresh.
#
# First playpick target ever aimed at whisper by name (0 hits for
# "boss":"whisper" in sessions.jsonl) and first priest:shadow pull this job
# has logged at all (0 hits for "spec":"priest:shadow"). whisper sits in
# room `oratory`, past marrow and THE CLIMB -- the walk has to cross THE
# VIGIL first, where #271/#281 already live; mash has stalled/wiped there
# once before (2026-09-24, druid:restoration, boss=crowns). This session
# is not chasing that bug again on purpose -- it is a new spec and a new
# target, and whatever happens in the VIGIL happens on the way.
open
targets
ui
shot front
tap raid
shot raid-setup
tap next
tap class:priest:shadow
shot class-selected
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
shot arrive-threshold
state
targets

# Chunk 1: threshold -> vigil -> spire(marrow) -> climb -> oratory(whisper).
# Generous budget; evening stops itself early (evening-stuck) if two rooms
# in a row go nowhere, which is exactly the failure mode being watched for.
evening mash 200 5
shot after-evening-1
state
says
bill
